[thin] The free edge ends the physically approved longer planar lead-in Derek requests across the rear caps. The taper approaches a mathematical point on the outside spring wall. The fitted spring section and solid retaining nose retain their approved geometry.
alternatives: A flat land removes the requested point. Thickening the spring changes the approved flexure; extending the nose changes the fitted catch. The requested point is integral with the full spring wall along the cap.
